# Citroen DS 19, Series 1, 1955-1962.
#
# The original DS, presented on 6 October 1955 and on sale in Britain from
# October 1955. The Series 1 ran to September 1962, when the range took the
# Series 2 restyle.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citro%C3%ABn_DS (Series 2 and Series 3 sections,
# cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.826 x 1.791 x 1.464 m, wheelbase 3.124 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes. The Autocar of October 1955 gives 4.801 x 1.791 x 1.473 m on a
# 3.124 m wheelbase; the 25 mm length difference is recorded in the pack, not
# resolved. The modelled hull is 4.826 m long on the published 3.124 m
# wheelbase, 1.791 m wide, 1.464 m high.
#
# Shape reference: a black car from the near side (about 8 degrees off a right
# angle, slightly blurred), a green car's front three-quarter and a cream and
# black car's rear. The defining features modelled are the teardrop body, the
# covered rear wheels with the narrower rear track, the thin-pillared cathedral
# roof with its wrap-around rear screen, and the smooth nose.
#
# **The Series 1 nose has open, exposed round headlamps in chrome bezels** with
# a small auxiliary lamp below each; the faired-in four-lamp glass canopy is the
# Series 3 restyle of late 1967, not 1962. The research pack established this on
# dated cars and from the maker's history, and the model follows it.
#
# Colours: no British-market colour list was found, so the objects carry plain
# names: black, white, red and blue. Weights black 3, white 3, red 2, blue 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase. Chrome is a separate
# material and is not affected by recolouring.
#
# Speed 140 km/h, the DS 19's quoted maximum, low for 1955 but matched to its
# long-stroke engine. Comfort 80/300, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 80: the
# hydropneumatic suspension and the seats made it one of the most comfortable
# cars of its era. Classes 2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: October 1955 intro, retires staggered 1975-1978 on a
# nineteen- to twenty-two-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/citroen-ds-1955.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/citroen-ds-1955.dae (57 objects). References:
# citycars/references/citroen-ds-1955/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the front bumper is slimmer and the rear-screen surround
# simpler than the photographs. Every glazing pane stands 15 mm clear of the
# local body surface. At 128 px the teardrop profile, the covered rear wheels
# and the exposed round lamps read as a Series 1 DS.

